jwnr_ltd@uhura.cc.rochester.edu (Joshua Winsor) writes:
{J} I just destroyed a room full of soldiers [and] I moved all of the armor
{J} and such to one spot ... in order to turn it into something more useful
{J} The problem is that ... the dungeon collapsed and my game was lost.

Yes.  That's one of the troubles with PCs, and there's not a whole lot to
do about it.  You could use exesmurf or exemod to modify the
/min(alloc) parm of the exe.  That would prevent the problem (to a
certain extent for you) in the future.  A "reasonable" number was
picked for distribution.

{J} What is the max. # of items that the system can handle (I am using PC
{J} nethack3.0j)?

Don't really know.  2 or 3 screens full is about the best answer.

The EXE has been told to leave a certain amount of memory free to allow
for grabbing of memory for items (read malloc()ing).  However you
can run out of free memory with too many items and crash the game.

Think of it as a tacit limitation on polypiling :-).

{J} 2: How do I get back into my game after the dungeon collapses?

You don't.  Sorry.

Maybe in 3.1 ...

